  "finding": "Reconciled the damage-healing discrepancy and formulated a physically consistent kinematic bulk-strain decomposition for nonmatching state transfer on Candidate C2 (h=0.0010 mm <= ell/3.75, 2,300 quads). Origin of the 0.0021837 healing artifact: authentic donor Package 50 node 231 has d=1.0021837 (+0.22% numerical overshoot above 1.0), which when transferred and clipped against upper bound 1.0 created an apparent healing of 0.0021837; physical lower bound d_lower = min(1.0, d_mapped) strictly satisfies pointwise irreversibility with max_physical_healing = 0.0 (PASS) while preserving authentic donor overshoot reporting. Replacing heuristic threshold zeroing (psi0_eff = 0 for d >= 0.95) with the kinematic bulk-strain decomposition eps_bulk = (1-d)^p eps (p=1, 2) suppresses spurious crack-opening strain surging from 974.55 kN/mm^2 down to 1.92 kN/mm^2 (p=1, -99.8%) and 0.03 kN/mm^2 (p=2, -99.99%) evaluated directly from bulk strain without threshold filtering. Coupled active-set PDAS converges in 2-3 iterations (vs 25 non-converged in baseline H1), discrete mechanical equilibrium residual is strictly preserved at 0.0 kN (<= 1e-10 kN target), fracture energy error is +2.49% (0.3037 mJ vs donor 0.2963 mJ), and reaction force is significantly restored to 4.14 N (+368% over threshold ablation's 0.88 N and +1033% over baseline's 0.36 N). Controlled mesh-resolution comparison (Package 72 -> C1 -> C2) confirms the coarse-donor hypothesis: fine-mesh Laplacian diffusion of the under-resolved donor profile (h_donor ~ ell/1.5) accounts for the remaining force deficit.",
